# Assignment 3.1 — Two-Page Website with Working Links

## Objective

To create a simple two-page website using HTML and connect the pages with working navigation links. The website will contain Home and About pages, along with an external website link that opens in a new tab.

## Solution

First, I opened Visual Studio Code and created a project folder named `two-page-website`. Inside the folder, I created two HTML files named `index.html` and `about.html`.

In the `index.html` file, I added the website name, an introduction, and a navigation bar containing Home and About links. I used the anchor (`a`) element with the `href` attribute to connect the two pages.

In the `about.html` file, I added information about the website and created the same navigation bar so that users could move between the Home and About pages.

I also added an external link to Google using `target="_blank"` to open it in a new tab. For security, I used `rel="noopener noreferrer"` with the external link.

Finally, I saved both files and opened `index.html` in a web browser. I tested the Home and About navigation links and verified that the external link opened in a new tab.

## 1. Home Page — index.html

Create a file named `index.html` and add the following code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Website - Home</title>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Website Header -->
    <header>
        <h1>My Website</h1>
        <p>Welcome to my first two-page website!</p>
    </header>

    <hr>

    <!-- Navigation Bar -->
    <nav>
        <a href="index.html">Home</a> |
        <a href="about.html">About</a>
    </nav>

    <hr>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main>
        <h2>Home Page</h2>
        <p>
            Welcome to my website. This website is created using HTML.
            It contains two pages connected through navigation links.
        </p>

        <p>
            You can visit the About page to learn more about this website.
        </p>

        <!-- External Website Link -->
        <p>
            Visit
            <a href="https://www.google.com/"
               target="_blank"
               rel="noopener noreferrer">
                Google
            </a>
            to explore the internet.
        </p>
    </main>

    <hr>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 My Website. All rights reserved.</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
```

